# INERT AS PLACED. Docker reads .dockerignore from the BUILD CONTEXT root, and
# docker/Dockerfile's context is the monorepo root — so this file is never
# consulted, and the equivalent belongs at the repo root instead. It is kept
# because it is the only record of what upstream excluded from its image, and
# because it becomes live again if anyone ever narrows the context back to this
# package.
#
# Upstream's exclusions, verbatim:
node_modules
dist
.git
test
docs
evidence
/tmp
